# The law rank/composition_image.sqlc owes: every combination of composed figures can be reached
# from the parts, so nothing on the fusion side is out of reach, and where something would be, a
# rule is already accusing somebody. Two rows.
#
# Nothing out of reach, stated as a count
#   Every declared fusion has its own parts, none shared and none empty, so each moves its composed
#   figure independently, and the number the parts can move is the number declared. Nothing is
#   left over on the fusion side, and that is the whole claim. The first subject holds it per
#   composition rather than for the corpus, because a composition is one filer's document.
#
# Which is why a declared fungibility has exactly one side to live on
#   Room on the part side is what a fusion asserts: supply moved between its parts leaves the
#   composed figure where it was. Room on the fusion side would be the opposite kind of fact, a
#   combination of composed figures no assignment to the parts can reach, and the model leaves
#   none. Only the part side is ever a claim.
#
# Inside, because it follows one way only
#   A composition with something out of reach has a declared fusion with no part under it, which
#   can only happen through a part that resolves to nothing, so checks/unresolved_part.sqlc is
#   already accusing that document. The other way does not follow: a fusion with one part that
#   resolves and one that does not still reaches its figure. So the second subject holds one set
#   inside the other and not the two equal, and writing them as equal would fail on the first
#   filing that loses one part of two.
#
# Zero is a rule holding it there, not the arithmetic coming out flat
#   It is the same as the layer graph's loops. Both counts are zero in every conforming document
#   because a rule refuses what would raise them, so a pass here is a statement about the rules
#   rather than about the numbers, and removing either rule gives this law something to say.
#
# Probe
#   examples/probes runs it as `composition_image` and `composition_image / the rule`. Delete the
#   filing identity a part names, and one composition must report something out of reach while the
#   rule reports the part; suppress the rule, and the second subject must fail with the count still
#   there.
-- rank/composition_image.sqlc, then the compositions with something out of reach against
-- checks/unresolved_part.sqlc.
SELECT a.slug AS law, p.subject, p.holds, p.detail
FROM      (
    :compose(algebra/roster.sqlc)
) a
LEFT JOIN (
    SELECT 'rank/composition_image' AS subject,
           count(*) > 0 AND sum(i.declared) > 0
           AND count(*) FILTER (WHERE i.declared <> i.rank + i.left_null) = 0
           AND sum(i.left_null) = 0                                                  AS holds,
           format('%s composition(s), %s declared fusion(s), %s within reach, %s out of reach%s',
                  count(*), sum(i.declared), sum(i.rank), sum(i.left_null),
                  coalesce(': ' || string_agg(i.composition, ', ' ORDER BY i.composition)
                                   FILTER (WHERE i.left_null > 0), ''))              AS detail
    FROM (
        :compose(rank/composition_image.sqlc)
    ) i
    UNION ALL
    SELECT 'rank/composition_image / the rule',
           count(*) FILTER (WHERE x.examined > 0) > 0
           AND count(*) FILTER (WHERE x.left_null > 0 AND x.accused = 0) = 0         AS holds,
           format('%s composition(s) have a fusion out of reach, %s of those have no part accused; '
                  '%s part reference(s) examined, %s accused%s',
                  count(*) FILTER (WHERE x.left_null > 0),
                  count(*) FILTER (WHERE x.left_null > 0 AND x.accused = 0),
                  sum(x.examined), sum(x.accused),
                  coalesce(': ' || string_agg(x.composition, ', ' ORDER BY x.composition)
                                   FILTER (WHERE x.left_null > 0 AND x.accused = 0), ''))
    FROM (
        SELECT i.composition, i.left_null,
               count(u.filing) FILTER (WHERE u.violates)             AS accused,
               count(u.filing) FILTER (WHERE u.violates IS NOT NULL) AS examined
        FROM      (
            :compose(rank/composition_image.sqlc)
        ) i
        LEFT JOIN (
            :compose(checks/unresolved_part.sqlc)
        ) u ON u.filing = i.composition
        GROUP BY i.composition, i.left_null
    ) x
) p ON true
WHERE a.slug = 'composition_image'
